"free" = "free";
"So a perfect game would score 1300 points (500 + 8 × 100), and every move and undo takes 1 point off. The Moves counter counts moves, undos and deals. In a won game with the usual 5 deals, your final score is 1305 minus the Moves counter: fewer moves, higher score." = "So a perfect game would score 1300 points (500 + 8 × 100), and every move and undo takes 1 point off. The Moves counter counts moves, undos and deals. In a won game with the usual 5 deals, your final score is 1305 minus the Moves counter: fewer moves, higher score.";
"Time" = "Time";
"The score box also shows how long you've played this game. The clock pauses while Spider Solitaire is in the background or a dialog is open, and it is saved with the game. Time doesn't change the score, but some achievements ask for a quick win." = "The score box also shows how long you've played this game. The clock pauses while Spider Solitaire is in the background or a dialog is open, and it is saved with the game. Time doesn't change the score, but some achievements ask for a quick win.";
"Tips" = "Tips";
"Ask for a hint" = "Ask for a hint";
"Choose Game ▸ Show Hint (⌘T) or click the score box. The cards that can move light up, then where they can go. Ask again to see the next idea. If there are no moves left, the game tells you." = "Choose Game ▸ Show Hint (⌘T) or click the score box. The cards that can move light up, then where they can go. Ask again to see the next idea. If there are no moves left, the game tells you.";
"Play winnable deals" = "Play winnable deals";
"Turn on \"Only deal winnable games\" in Settings and every new game is one a built-in solver has already won. It usually takes a moment at most; with four suits it can take a few seconds." = "Turn on \"Only deal winnable games\" in Settings and every new game is one a built-in solver has already won. It usually takes a moment at most; with four suits it can take a few seconds.";
"Undo the way you like" = "Undo the way you like";
"Undo (⌘Z) can go back to the start of the game, and Redo (⇧⌘Z) brings moves back. For a stricter game, choose Classic XP undo in Settings: then undo stops at each deal and each completed suit, like the original." = "Undo (⌘Z) can go back to the start of the game, and Redo (⇧⌘Z) brings moves back. For a stricter game, choose Classic XP undo in Settings: then undo stops at each deal and each completed suit, like the original.";
"A few strategy ideas" = "A few strategy ideas";
